From: NWA50BE OpenWrt Project <noreply@invalid.example>
Subject: [PATCH] luci: use a private ubus connection in forked uhttpd workers
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

uhttpd loads the ucode handler in its main process, so luci.dispatcher
opens its ubus connection there, and every forked worker inherits that
socket while the parent keeps watching it in its event loop. When a worker
sends a ubus call, the parent can read the reply first and drop it, and
the worker then waits forever. On the NWA50BE (four CPUs) every request
that reached a ubus call, including the login page, hung its worker, and
the stuck workers blocked all later requests. Pinning the process to one
CPU hid it, which is how it was found.

Connect again at the start of each dispatch so the worker owns the socket
it waits on.

---
--- a/modules/luci-base/ucode/dispatcher.uc
+++ b/modules/luci-base/ucode/dispatcher.uc
@@ -882,6 +882,10 @@
 dispatch = function(_http, path) {
 	http = _http;
 
+	// The uhttpd parent preloads this module and watches its ubus socket in
+	// its event loop; use a private connection in the forked worker.
+	ubus = connect();
+
 	let version = determine_version();
 	let lang = determine_request_language();
 
